      "content_preview_first_1200": "# Galaxy Evolution\n\n> Reader note: Highlighted claim chips open the existing provenance layer. This article summarizes current evidence while keeping debated mechanisms visible; trust badges, trust scores, evidence rows, votes, and thresholds are unchanged.\n\n## Overview & Historical Framework\n\nGalaxy evolution connects the growth of dark-matter halos to the visible history of stars, gas, dust, black holes, and environment. The modern picture is not a single sequence from blue spirals to red ellipticals; it is a set of coupled channels. Halos assemble hierarchically, gas accretes and cools, star formation consumes and enriches that gas, feedback redistributes energy and metals, and dense environments can remove or heat reservoirs before galaxies would have quenched on their own.\n\nThe red sequence, green valley, and blue cloud remain useful observational landmarks, but they are outcomes rather than mechanisms. A reader-facing synthesis should therefore start with causal structure: what sets the baryon supply, what regulates star formation, what shuts galaxies down, and which observations distinguish internal feedback from external processing.\n\n<!-- claim:2931-->Galaxy quenching is jo",
