          "id": 2930,
          "order_idx": 2,
          "section": "Star Formation & Quenching",
          "text": "Gas removal and depletion can suppress star formation by reducing the usable cold-gas reservoir, but the evidence should distinguish true reservoir loss from morphological quenching, turbulent regulation, and environment-specific stripping.",
